1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:04,054
You cannot protect what you cannot find.

2
00:00:04,054 --> 00:00:09,192
Forgotten subdomains. Expired certificates. Cloud resources nobody owns.

3
00:00:12,192 --> 00:00:14,814
What does your attack surface look like to an

4
00:00:14,814 --> 00:00:17,669
attacker, right now? In this course you build the

5
00:00:17,669 --> 00:00:20,349
platform that answers that question every day,

6
00:00:20,349 --> 00:00:23,088
without ever stepping outside authorized scope.

7
00:00:26,088 --> 00:00:29,976
Gennoor Tech presents Agentic Attack Surface Management.

8
00:00:32,976 --> 00:00:36,254
Discover. Reconcile. Assign. Five sources,

9
00:00:36,254 --> 00:00:39,141
D N S, certificates, cloud inventory,

10
00:00:39,141 --> 00:00:41,404
C M D B and scanner findings,

11
00:00:41,404 --> 00:00:44,370
reconciled into one owned asset graph.

12
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:49,209
Every record carries provenance. Every uncertain match goes to

13
00:00:49,209 --> 00:00:53,345
a review queue. And every discovery action is checked

14
00:00:53,345 --> 00:00:55,608
against scope before it runs.

15
00:00:58,608 --> 00:01:00,706
Day one starts with authorization,

16
00:01:00,706 --> 00:01:03,669
because weak scope is the biggest risk in attack

17
00:01:03,669 --> 00:01:06,199
surface tooling. You write the allowlist,

18
00:01:06,199 --> 00:01:09,408
the exclusions, the rate limits and the audit trail,

19
00:01:09,408 --> 00:01:12,617
and you prove that an out-of-scope target is blocked

20
00:01:12,617 --> 00:01:13,296
and logged.

21
00:01:16,296 --> 00:01:18,406
Then the five source adapters,

22
00:01:18,406 --> 00:01:23,259
fixture-based and testable, and a normalized inventory with canonical

23
00:01:23,259 --> 00:01:25,510
asset I Ds, first and last seen,

24
00:01:25,510 --> 00:01:28,464
confidence, environment and relationships.

25
00:01:31,464 --> 00:01:36,889
Day two is reconciliation. Entity resolution uses deterministic signals,

26
00:01:36,889 --> 00:01:39,451
exact hostname, certificate S A N,

27
00:01:39,451 --> 00:01:42,616
cloud resource I D and verified ownership.

28
00:01:42,616 --> 00:01:45,630
Anything uncertain is queued for review,

29
00:01:45,630 --> 00:01:49,021
never silently merged. Then change detection:

30
00:01:49,021 --> 00:01:52,261
snapshot to snapshot, you find what is new,

31
00:01:52,261 --> 00:01:54,974
changed, missing, stale or orphaned,

32
00:01:54,974 --> 00:01:58,440
validated against fixtures with known answers.

33
00:02:01,440 --> 00:02:04,002
Then exposure. Assets join to findings,

34
00:02:04,002 --> 00:02:06,761
service metadata and business criticality,

35
00:02:06,761 --> 00:02:09,191
and an agent summarizes the exposure.

36
00:02:09,191 --> 00:02:12,279
It must separate what was observed from what it

37
00:02:12,279 --> 00:02:15,432
inferred, and you measure how often it fails to.

38
00:02:18,432 --> 00:02:20,882
Day three is ownership and action.

39
00:02:20,882 --> 00:02:22,756
Synthetic C M D B records,

40
00:02:22,756 --> 00:02:26,792
tags and repository metadata suggest a responsible team,

41
00:02:26,792 --> 00:02:30,684
with evidence attached and manual correction built in.

42
00:02:30,684 --> 00:02:35,512
Transparent ranking raises review tickets through a mock connector.

43
00:02:35,512 --> 00:02:37,530
And you publish the metrics:

44
00:02:37,530 --> 00:02:40,053
link precision, unowned asset rate,

45
00:02:40,053 --> 00:02:43,728
stale classification and change-detection accuracy.

46
00:02:46,728 --> 00:02:50,344
Every lab uses fixture sources and lab-owned domains,

47
00:02:50,344 --> 00:02:53,756
so the discovery you practise is real in technique

48
00:02:53,756 --> 00:02:54,984
and safe in scope.

49
00:02:57,984 --> 00:03:00,622
Here is the full table of contents,

50
00:03:00,622 --> 00:03:02,581
9 modules over three days.

51
00:03:02,581 --> 00:03:06,273
Day one: Authorization, scope policy and the lab;

52
00:03:06,273 --> 00:03:10,719
Source adapters; and Asset normalization and canonical IDs.

53
00:03:10,719 --> 00:03:14,111
Day two: Entity resolution; Change detection;

54
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:17,049
and Exposure correlation with an agent.

55
00:03:17,049 --> 00:03:20,667
Day three: Ownership resolution; Prioritization,

56
00:03:20,667 --> 00:03:23,681
ticketing and inventory quality metrics;

57
00:03:23,681 --> 00:03:27,072
and Capstone: scoped attack surface platform.

58
00:03:30,072 --> 00:03:34,244
Every build in this course follows six engineering principles.

59
00:03:34,244 --> 00:03:36,060
Model output is a proposal,

60
00:03:36,060 --> 00:03:39,559
never a fact. Authorization lives outside the model.

61
00:03:39,559 --> 00:03:42,519
A human approves every consequential action.

62
00:03:42,519 --> 00:03:44,807
Decisions and evidence are logged.

63
00:03:44,807 --> 00:03:48,777
The stack stays provider-agnostic. And quality is measured,

64
00:03:48,777 --> 00:03:49,584
not assumed.

65
00:03:52,584 --> 00:03:54,962
Five asset sources. Three days,

66
00:03:54,962 --> 00:03:59,640
hands-on. Zero out-of-scope discovery. One owned asset graph.

